## 11. Open questions

- Q1: the PLAN row says the piece has six edges while the briefing edge set and the degree sum both give seven, and the spec draws seven. Evidence that would settle it: a corrected roster line, or a review naming which edge is meant to be dropped.
- Q2: view B reuses the five arcs of 9.2.2, so {a,b} and {a,t} appear in A and not in B. Should B instead mirror all seven edges as arc pairs? Evidence: a ruling that one arc set serves the whole chapter, which would also change FIG-09-04.
- Q3: no rendered frame exists, so the two reduced scales are unverified by eye. Evidence: a G1 thumbnail at 10:9, where a 15.4 radius disc and an 18-unit id are checked for fit.

